<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yoga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yoga is a group of physical, mental and spiritual practices that originated in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, aimed at controlling body and mind to attain liberation (moksha), as practised in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a>, Jain and Buddhist traditions. It may have pre-Vedic origins but is first attested in the early first millennium BCE, and systematic yoga concepts emerged in the fifth and sixth centuries BCE in the ascetic and Śramaṇa movements. The Yoga Sutras of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patanjali">Patanjali</a>, the classical text on Hindu yoga, date to the early centuries of the Common Era, and hatha yoga texts appeared between the ninth and 11th centuries. Modern forms, largely made up of asanas, spread worldwide after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swami-vivekananda">Swami Vivekananda</a>'s adaptation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yoga.jpg" alt="Yoga" width="330" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Company School · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bharadwaja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Practices of yoga and meditation, rooted in Hindu traditions and the <b>Yoga</b> Sutras of Patanjali, have spread worldwide in adapted forms, and Gandhi’s non-violent resistance, inspired in part by the Bhagavad Gita, shaped movements for civil rights across the world.</blockquote><a href="/religion/hinduism">Hinduism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>The old ritual survived in the Śrauta tradition, while <b>Yoga</b> and Vedanta acknowledged the authority of the Vedas but read the Vedic pantheon as a unitary view of the universe, with Brahman both immanent and transcendent.</blockquote><a href="/culture/vedic-civilisation">Vedic civilisation · Legacy</a></li></ul></section>
